# Rank 1197 / CVE-2025-48057: icinga2's VerifyCertificate in
# lib/base/tlsutility.cpp built a fresh X509_STORE from the caller-supplied
# CA certificate on every call and verified the caller-supplied leaf
# certificate against it, which reads as a correct, stateless verification at
# every call site (CWE-295). The defect is inside OpenSSL itself when built
# against a version older than 1.1.0: those releases cache a "valid" flag on
# the X509 struct the first time it passes X509_verify_cert, and a later call
# that reuses the same in-memory X509* for a second verification -- against a
# different CA store, exactly what icinga2 does when re-checking a peer's
# certificate against a rotated or per-endpoint trust anchor -- short-circuits
# on that cached flag and returns valid without re-walking the chain against
# the new store at all. Confirmed against the diff at 60f75f4a3d: the flag and
# the short-circuit it drives live entirely inside OpenSSL's own
# X509_verify_cert (removed upstream in openssl/openssl@0e76014e for 1.1.0),
# not in any icinga2 source.
#
# ATTENTION, no taint path, fails the genericity test. vyql match on
# tlsutility.cpp labels nothing at VerifyCertificate, X509_STORE_CTX_init or
# X509_verify_cert -- no source, no sink, nothing for a rule to consume -- and
# scanning the real checkout at both revisions (icinga/icinga2, both cpp:637
# files) reports the same VYQL-CRY-001/VYQL-LIFE-001/VYQL-MEM-002 findings
# elsewhere in the file, unrelated to this function, identically before and
# after. There is nothing to trace because the bug is not a dataflow relation
# between two values in icinga2's own code: every call site of
# VerifyCertificate is byte-identical at both revisions, and the
# vulnerable and patched forms of the function itself differ only in a
# preprocessor-guarded block (`#if OPENSSL_VERSION_NUMBER < 0x10100000L`)
# whose necessity is documented nowhere but OpenSSL's own change history --
# not in X509_verify_cert's man page, not in any usage guidance a binding
# could be written from. A rule narrow enough to require "certificate object
# gets serialized and reparsed before its second verification" would match
# only this one function's workaround (AGENTS.md's genericity test: nobody
# reading OpenSSL's public documentation would write that binding without
# having seen this CVE), and a rule broad enough to flag "certificate reused
# across two verification calls" has no source location to anchor on -- both
# revisions call VerifyCertificate the same way from the same call sites, so
# the only distinguishing fact is a build-time macro no static source scan
# evaluates. No definition change attempted; not an engine gap either, since
# the engine's taint model has no missing edge here to add -- there is no
# edge to have.
#
# verify_current_expected: attention-no-taint-path

test "rank1197: VerifyCertificate builds and checks a fresh store against the caller's certificate directly"
  lang cpp
  file lib/base/tlsutility.cpp
  reject VYQL-CFG-004
  code
  ```
  bool VerifyCertificate(X509* caCertificate, X509* certificate, const String& crlFile)
  {
    std::unique_ptr<X509_STORE, decltype(&X509_STORE_free)> store{X509_STORE_new(), &X509_STORE_free};

    if (!store)
      return false;

    X509_STORE_add_cert(store.get(), caCertificate);

    if (!crlFile.IsEmpty()) {
      AddCRLToSSLContext(store.get(), crlFile);
    }

    std::unique_ptr<X509_STORE_CTX, decltype(&X509_STORE_CTX_free)> csc{X509_STORE_CTX_new(), &X509_STORE_CTX_free};
    X509_STORE_CTX_init(csc.get(), store.get(), certificate, nullptr);

    int rc = X509_verify_cert(csc.get());

    return rc == 1;
  }
  ```

test "rank1197: fix re-serializes the certificate under old OpenSSL before the same store check"
  lang cpp
  file lib/base/tlsutility.cpp
  reject VYQL-CFG-004
  code
  ```
  bool VerifyCertificate(X509* caCertificate, X509* certificate, const String& crlFile)
  {
  #if OPENSSL_VERSION_NUMBER < 0x10100000L
    std::shared_ptr<X509> copy = StringToCertificate(CertificateToString(certificate));
    VERIFY(copy.get() != certificate);
    certificate = copy.get();
  #endif

    std::unique_ptr<X509_STORE, decltype(&X509_STORE_free)> store{X509_STORE_new(), &X509_STORE_free};

    if (!store)
      return false;

    X509_STORE_add_cert(store.get(), caCertificate);

    if (!crlFile.IsEmpty()) {
      AddCRLToSSLContext(store.get(), crlFile);
    }

    std::unique_ptr<X509_STORE_CTX, decltype(&X509_STORE_CTX_free)> csc{X509_STORE_CTX_new(), &X509_STORE_CTX_free};
    X509_STORE_CTX_init(csc.get(), store.get(), certificate, nullptr);

    int rc = X509_verify_cert(csc.get());

    return rc == 1;
  }
  ```
